# N-1 evidence: tap native / see native reach the Android system Share
# sheet — a fully native UI surface with no Flutter widget tree at all,
# triggered here via an external ACTION_SEND intent (not by tapping
# anything inside water-sip, since water-sip has no share flow of its own —
# this proves the mechanism against a genuine native UI regardless).
#
# No "restart the app" in a before-hook here — that would dismiss the
# already-open native share sheet this test depends on.

test "see native and tap native locate real elements in the Android share sheet"
  see native "Chrome"
  see native "Gmail"
  don't see native "Nonexistent App XYZ 12345"
  tap native "Bluetooth"
  wait 2 seconds
  take a screenshot called "n1_after_tap_native_bluetooth"
